2026-09-04T09:06:39Z cd /home/ritz/code/crates/nsi
git add -A -- ':!repro_shared' && git status --porcelain && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'
Make Arg::array_len take a NonZeroUsize

`get_c_param_vec` computes `count` as `data.len() / array_length`, so
`array_len(0)` reached a division by zero while forming `NSIParam`.

Model the invariant in the type instead of checking it: `array_length`
becomes a `NonZeroUsize` (defaulting to `NonZeroUsize::MIN`) and the
public `array_len` takes one. `usize / NonZeroUsize` is std's panic-free
`Div` impl, so the division site is unchanged and a zero divisor is no
longer expressible.

Breaking: call sites pass `const { NonZeroUsize::new(N).unwrap() }`,
which rejects a literal zero at compile time with no runtime branch.

Adds two unit tests covering the element-count arithmetic the divisor
guards; they need no renderer present.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01N9BGWukJmJZEk9Ez5eNSX6
EOF
